<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">United Provinces of Central Italy</h1><p class="st-meta">1859 CE – 1860 CE · capital Modena</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A short-lived union of Tuscany, Modena, Parma and Romagna formed in 1859, which voted to join Piedmont and paved the way for Italian unity.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>During the war of 1859 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> and the alliance of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-sardinia">Kingdom of Sardinia</a>, the rulers of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/grand-duchy-of-tuscany">Grand Duchy of Tuscany</a>, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-modena-and-reggio">Duchy of Modena and Reggio</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-parma-and-piacenza">Duchy of Parma and Piacenza</a> fled, and the papal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romagna">Legations of Romagna</a> rebelled. Their provisional governments formed a league with a common army under General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manfredo-fanti">Manfredo Fanti</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The union was a military and political alliance rather than a full state. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luigi-carlo-farini">Luigi Carlo Farini</a> governed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/modena">Modena</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-parma-and-piacenza">Parma</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romagna">Romagna</a>, united as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emilia">Emilia</a>, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bettino-ricasoli">Bettino Ricasoli</a> led <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/grand-duchy-of-tuscany">Tuscany</a>. Their assemblies voted to join the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-sardinia">Kingdom of Sardinia</a>, defying the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armistice-of-villafranca">Peace of Villafranca</a>, which had foreseen the return of the old rulers.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After plebiscites in March 1860, the territories were annexed to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-sardinia">Kingdom of Sardinia</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> receiving <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nice">Nice</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-savoy">Savoy</a> in exchange. They became part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-italy">Kingdom of Italy</a> in 1861.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/united-provinces-of-central-italy.jpg" alt="United Provinces of Central Italy" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: F l a n k e r · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Italy_(1861-1946)_crowned_simplified.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1859 CE – 1860 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Modena</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Luigi Carlo Farini, Bettino Ricasoli</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Italian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Province Unite del Centro Italia</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1860&amp;focus=united-provinces-of-central-italy" aria-label="United Provinces of Central Italy on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4941 599 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where United Provinces of Central Italy lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5261 855L5270 883M5261 855L5261 855M5261 855L5246 851M5261 855L5226 1028"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5270 883h0M5261 855h0M5246 851h0M5226 1028h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5261 855h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5261 855h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Modena. <a href="/atlas?year=1860&amp;focus=united-provinces-of-central-italy">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
